.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.TH OCTA-CONTROL 1 "" "OCTA-CAPTURE @PROJECT_VERSION@" "OCTA-CAPTURE Manual"
.SH NAME
octa\-control \- set a preamp or compressor parameter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBocta-control\fR [\fB\-\-dry-run\fR] CHANNEL PARAMETER VALUE [CTRL-PORT]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set one input parameter and print the freshly read device state as JSON.
\fB\-\-dry-run\fR emits frame_hex JSON without opening hardware.
Channels are numbered 1 through 8. Hi-Z uses only 1/2; stereo-link uses 1/3/5/7.
.PP
Parameters and index bounds are:
phantom, low-cut, phase, hi-z, stereo-link, compressor (0/1);
sensitivity (0..100), gate (0..50), attack (0..25), release (0..45),
threshold (0..50), ratio (0..8), gain (0..74).
Attack, release and ratio use fixed lookup tables.
Phantom and Hi-Z change physical input conditions.
.PP
Arguments use decimal wire indices or coefficients rather than displayed units.
Run as the regular user with access to the ALSA device.
.PP
The default CTRL MIDI port is hw:CARD=OCTACAPTURE,DEV=0,SUBDEV=1. Close other control-panel/CTRL clients before opening it. Audio streaming is independent of this connection.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success; nonzero indicates a usage, device or operation error.
.SH SEE ALSO
octa-capture(1), octa-status(1), octa-preset(1)
